1. WHAT YOU MAY DO, FREE
   You may use GEditor, copy it, change it and build new things on top of it, for any purpose, including editing videos
   that earn you money (your own reels, client work, ads). The videos you make are yours. GEditor takes no share of them.

2. WHAT MUST STAY
   a. The name "GEditor" must stay on GEditor and on anything that contains a substantial part of it. You may not rename it
      or present it under another name.
   b. The credit "GEditor by GauthamWho" and this licence file must stay in every copy, and your changed or extended
      version must show that credit where users can see it (for example in the About / README and the app's title area).
   c. You may say your project is "built on GEditor". You may not say it is made or endorsed by GauthamWho.

3. WHAT NEEDS A PAID DEAL WITH THE AUTHOR
   You may not sell GEditor, or sell, rent, host-for-a-fee or charge subscriptions for GEditor, an app or service built from
   it, or anything that contains a substantial part of its code, unless you first make a separate written paid agreement
   with the author (GitHub: GauthamWho). Editing your own paid videos with GEditor does NOT need a deal (see 1).

4. THIRD-PARTY PARTS
   GEditor uses other free software that keeps its own licences (see NOTICE.md). This licence covers only the GEditor code.

5. NO WARRANTY
   GEditor is provided "as is", without any warranty. The author is not liable for any loss or damage from using it.

6. ENDING
   If you break this licence, your permission under it ends until you fix the breach.
